# Rust build output
/target

# Per-user CRIME state when dogfooding CRIME on this repo.
# Config is committable; state is not. See F9 in docs/example-map.md.
.crime/state.json

# Agent worktrees: a full checkout plus its build output, 2.3 GB of it.
.claude/worktrees/
# Per-user agent settings; the shared contract is CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Derived per-user Risk data when dogfooding CRIME on this repo: the figure
# cache, the Refactor loop's per-Iteration snapshots and its completion
# sentinel. Unlike reviews and stories these are computed, not authored, and
# they change on every commit — a committed cache is a merge conflict in a file
# nobody reads by hand. See F27 in docs/example-map.md.
.crime/risk.json
.crime/snapshots/
.crime/refactor-done

# One transcript per language server, written by the edge while dogfooding.
# Derived, per-user and per-session, for the same reason the Risk cache above is.
.crime/lsp-*.log
